@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# Overwatch server — dashboard & notifications
+
+`@overwatch/server` is the operator interface for Overwatch. It ingests browser
+error events (the same endpoint `@overwatch/browser` posts to), folds them into
+persistent incidents via `@overwatch/triage`, serves a web dashboard, and sends
+Slack/Discord notifications routed by owning team.
+
+Zero runtime dependencies; Node 22+. The triage engine is imported directly
+from `../triage` (same repo) — if you split packages, depend on
+`@overwatch/triage` instead.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+node server/src/index.js --config server/overwatch.config.example.json
+# or from the repo root:
+npm run server
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:8090`. Configuration is `defaults < JSON file < env vars`
+(`OVERWATCH_PORT`, `OVERWATCH_STORE`, `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`,
+`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`, `OVERWATCH_PUBLIC_URL`). See
+`overwatch.config.example.json`. Set `storePath` to persist incidents across
+restarts (debounced JSON writes); without it the store is in-memory.
+
+Point the browser SDK at this server:
+
+```js
+init({ endpoint: 'http://localhost:8090/v1/events', projectId: 'my-site' });
+```
+
+## API
+
+| Method | Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| POST | `/v1/events` | Ingest a schema-v1 event envelope (SDK endpoint) |
+| GET | `/api/incidents?status=active,acknowledged` | List incident summaries (`all` for everything) |
+| GET | `/api/incidents/:id` | Full report: assessment, evidence, timeline, latest events |
+| POST | `/api/incidents/:id/acknowledge` | `{by, note?}` — mark as being handled |
+| POST | `/api/incidents/:id/resolve` | `{by, note?}` — mark resolved |
+| POST | `/api/incidents/:id/reopen` | Manually reopen a resolved incident |
+| POST | `/api/reports` | Manual report form: `{title, description, page?, reporter?, severity?}` |
+| GET | `/api/health` | Health check |
+
+## Incident lifecycle
+
+`active → acknowledged → resolved`. New events matching a resolved incident
+automatically reopen it with a timeline entry. Every transition, event batch,
+severity change and notification attempt is recorded on the incident timeline.
+
+## Notifications
+
+Incidents recommending `escalate` or `investigate` notify a webhook (`observe`
+only when `notifyObserved: true`). Routing: `notify.routes` matches the assessed
+owner's `team` or `service`, falling back to the global `slack`/`discord`
+webhook. Escalating incidents send an urgent variant (`@here` on Discord).
+Repeat notifications for the same incident + recommendation are suppressed for
+`cooldownMs` (default 30 min); a severity change re-notifies because the
+recommendation changes. Failures are logged on the timeline, not retried.
+
+Webhook detection: `type: 'slack'|'discord'` or inferred from the URL. Payloads
+include severity, event count, estimated users, owner, action and a dashboard
+link (`publicUrl + #incident-id`).
+
+## Dashboard
+
+Vanilla JS, no build step. Filter tabs (Open/Active/Acknowledged/Resolved/All),
+auto-refresh every 10s, click a card for the full report: summary, the four
+triage assessments with evidence, timeline, latest events, and acknowledge /
+resolve controls. `+ Report issue` opens the manual submission form. Deep links:
+`/#incident-inc-xxxx`.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+node --test server/test/*.test.js     # API, lifecycle, notifications, dedupe, reopen
+npx playwright test -c server/playwright.config.js   # e2e: boots the server, drives the UI
+```
